# Changelog (released versions are frozen)

[CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) follows Keep a Changelog. Dated `## [x.y.z]`
sections are **immutable**.

**CHANGELOG = product. Website ≠ product.** Do not add, date, or “complete
a release” with website notes.

Website is `website/**` (Astro/Starlight source and the npm package in that
tree), `.github/workflows/pages.yml`, Pages artifacts (`website/dist/`,
cicerone.dev chrome), and anything that exists only to publish
cicerone.dev. `docs/*.md` is not website-only (see Borderline).

Product is the `cicerone` package: job, serve, dashboard app, events, I/O,
CLI, config, models.

If a train has both product and site changes, Unreleased gets **only**
the product bullets — no website bullet beside them. Site-only: leave
Unreleased empty (no placeholder).

Split lives only in this file. Keep the `changelog.mdc` line in
[agent-policy-source.mdc](agent-policy-source.mdc) in sync; do not fork a
second copy of the split.

## Borderline

- Logo / dashboard CSS in `src/cicerone/static/`: product. The same asset
  only under `website/`: not.
- `docs/*.md` or OpenAPI copied onto the site: changelog the **package**
  change. A site-only rewrite of those pages: not.

## Do

- Put new notes only under `## [Unreleased]` on the train you are
  targeting (patch on `main`, minor on `release/X.Y.0`).
- Short bullets for **this** product change. Do not re-tell older releases.

## Do not

- Changelog the website. Ever.
- Edit, rewrite, move, or “clarify” any `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section.
- Expand Unreleased bullets so they re-document a shipped version
  (e.g. do not narrate 0.5.0 lock behavior inside a later HA note).
- Backport Unreleased items into an already-tagged release section.
